-- title:
--   Frobenius pin: ̄ a₀^{ q} equals the moduli value at a supersingular place
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a natural number $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A,M')$ over the residue field $\kappa_A=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\ q\ M'\ \kappa_A$ (rational, affine geometric, and with $\mathrm{jGeomGen}$ evaluating into $\mathrm{ssJSet}\ q\ \kappa_A$), and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of the base change $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A,M')$, compatible with coefficientwise reduction: each Laurent series over $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((\mathsf q))$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ is $R_0$-integral, with $R_0$-residue given by applying $\mathrm{residue}\ A$ to its coefficients. Let $s\in W$. Let $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}$, $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element of $A$, and assume $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$. Let $\ell'$ be a prime with $\ell'\ge 3$, $\ell'\neq q$, $\ell'\nmid M'$, and let $K_\ell\subseteq k_0((\mathsf q))$ be the base change to $k_0$ of $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ for the subgroup $\mathrm{levelH}\ (q\ell')\ M'$ (the kernel of the reduction map of unit groups), equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $k_0$. Let $j_\ell\in K_\ell$ be the nonzero element whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of $\mathrm{jq}$, let $C=\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\ A_0\ K_\ell\ j_\ell$ be the subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$, and let $y\subseteq C$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $\pi_0$ and supersingular in the sense that every ring homomorphism from $C$ onto an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with kernel $y$ sends $\mathrm{jChartFin}$ into $\mathrm{ssJSet}\ q$ of that field. Assume moreover (hypothesis `hover`) that $y$ computes values at $s$: for every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ whose base change is $R_0$-integral, whose order is nonnegative at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ at which $j$ has nonnegative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa_A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the element of $C$ obtained from $\mathrm{qExpand}\ k_0\ \ell'$ applied to the coefficientwise image of $g$ differs from the image of $c$ by an element of $y$. Finally let $\mathrm{jqNModC}\ k_0\ (q\ell')$ lie in $K_\ell$ and in $C$, and let $a_0\in A_0$ be such that this element minus the image of $a_0$ lies in $y$. The conclusion is that, granting that the base change of $\mathrm{jq}$ to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is $R_0$-integral and that $a_0$ lies in $A$, one has $(\mathrm{residue}\ A\ a_0)^q = s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}\ j)$ in $\kappa_A$.
--
--   This is the Frobenius normalisation at a supersingular point: the reduction modulo $y$ of the lift $j(\mathsf q^{q\ell'})$ is a $q$-th root of the value at $s$ of the reduced moduli invariant, obtained from Kronecker's congruence for the modular polynomial $\Phi_q$ together with the fact that supersingular $j$-invariants satisfy $j^{q^2}=j$. It feeds the construction of a common chart with prescribed nodes and separation data in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_fixedField_of_rigidChart_ends`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_fixedField_of_rigidChart_ends).
